{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>וירף.</b> דמים in the sacred language has two senses: the first, shedding of blood, as in \"איש דמים אתה לי\" (2 Samuel 16:8), and the commentator who says it means life is wrong; the second, a plural of actual blood, as in \"בדמיך חיי\" (Ezekiel 16:6). Now she said, upon seeing that the illness had departed from Moses: You are no longer a חתן דמים in the sense of killing, but rather a bridegroom immersed in the blood of circumcision. מולות is there a noun. And it is in the plural on account of דמים."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:49.280428996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}